menu "EPub-InkPlate Storage"

    config USE_SD_CARD
        bool "Use SD card for storage (book, fonts, cache)"
        default n
        help
            When enabled, the firmware reads the book, fonts, and pagination
            cache from a microSD card mounted at /sdcard (original behaviour).

            When disabled (default for single_book builds), the firmware uses
            a LittleFS partition in flash mounted at /littlefs. The partition
            label is "storage" and must be flashed separately with:

              esptool.py --chip esp32 -p PORT write_flash 0x310000 build_single/storage.bin

            The LittleFS image is built automatically by CMake from the
            littlefs_root/ directory in the repository. Populate that
            directory with the book, fonts, and fonts_list.xml before
            building.

endmenu
